Note the retry/idempotency path in the same file (lines 165–177) does this correctly by re-deriving `seatNumbers` from `seatNumbersInLegOrder(passenger)` on each passenger object directly (correlated by identity, not index) — the fix is to do the same in the creation-return path, e.g. build the seat assignments in memory from `protectedPassengers`/`passengers` (already correlated by construction) instead of round-tripping through the unordered `booking.passengers` include, or add an explicit `orderBy` plus a match by `id` rather than array position.

No other large/obvious bugs (off-by-one, inverted conditions, null derefs, wrong SQL, control-flow breaks) were found in the rest of the diff — the `cancelBookingAction`/`changeBookingSeatsAction` rewrites, the `ProfileClient`/`AdminFlightsTable` cabin lookups, and the migration's orphan-check SQL all correlate data by ID/leg-sequence rather than raw array position, and look correct.

